    "body": "CSS, in particular, [explicitly calls out hash-only urls](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#local-urls) (that is, values of the `url()` function that start with a hash) as always being local.  They still resolve to absolute URLs as normal, but they have an internal \"local url\" flag set, forcing them to serialize as hash-only, and making them always be interpreted as references to the current document only.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
